{
  "format": "pantherclaw.conformance/v1",
  "group": "wrappers",
  "description": "How a framework wrapper (LangChain/LangGraph, OpenAI Agents SDK, CrewAI, Vercel AI SDK, MCP TypeScript SDK) decides each call of a wrapped tool through the /sdk face: only allow lets the tool run, a hold is waited on and the identical call resubmitted, an identical retry of a held call reuses its action id, and every other outcome returns a refusal to the model (or raises, with raise_on_refusal) without running the tool. The fake gateway answers each /sdk request with the case's next answer, rewritten for the PC-Action-Id it received: action_id and every occurrence of the file's action_id in the decoded action_ir are replaced, and action_hash becomes the SHA-256 of the rewritten action_ir when it was the SHA-256 of the original.",
  "source": "the framework wrappers' contract (M14 PN-016.3, HR-328, HR-329) over the /sdk face answers of sdk_face.json (internal/gateway/sdk), internal/actionir for hashes, internal/authority/finalize for the action token and internal/gen protojson for the waits",
